      "text": [
        ": سَأَلَ رَجُلٌ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ وَ أَنَا حَاضِرٌ عَنْ رَجُلٍ ضَرَبَ رَجُلاً فَلَمْ يَنْقَطِعْ بَوْلُهُ قَالَ \"إِنْ كَانَ اَلْبَوْلُ يَمُرُّ إِلَى اَللَّيْلِ فَعَلَيْهِ اَلدِّيَةُ وَ إِنْ كَانَ إِلَى نِصْفِ اَلنَّهَارِ فَعَلَيْهِ ثُلُثَا اَلدِّيَةِ وَ إِنْ كَانَ إِلَى اِرْتِفَاعِ اَلنَّهَارِ فَعَلَيْهِ ثُلُثُ اَلدِّيَةِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5314 - It was narrated from Ishaq ibn Ammar that he said:\nA man asked Abu Abdullah (as), while I was present, about a man who struck another man, causing his urine to flow continuously without stopping.\nImam (as) said: \"If the urine continues until the night, then the full blood money (diyyah) is due. If it continues until midday, then two-thirds of the blood money is due. If it continues only until the morning rises, then one-third of the blood money is due.\""
        ]
      }
